  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07772v3</id>
    <title>An approach for systematic decomposition of complex llm tasks</title>
    <updated>2026-01-18T18:47:31Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07772v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.07772v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Large Language Models (LLMs) suffer from reliability issues on complex tasks, as existing decomposition methods are heuristic and rely on agent or manual decomposition. This work introduces a novel, systematic decomposition framework that we call Analysis of CONstraint-Induced Complexity (ACONIC), which models the task as a constraint problem and leverages formal complexity measures to guide decomposition. On combinatorial (SAT-Bench) and LLM database querying tasks (Spider), we find that by decomposing the tasks following the measure of complexity, agent can perform considerably better.</summary>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-10-09T04:24:47Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.AI"/>
    <author>
